  "id": "attachment-style",
  "term": "attachment style",
  "definition": "Attachment style is a way of describing how a person relates in attachment terms, often using labels such as secure, avoidant, anxious, or fearful-avoidant. In this source, it is treated as a dimensional, changeable pattern rather than a fixed type, shaped by life experiences, emotional regulation, and social context.",
